# Google Calendar + Meet

- Calendar connection uses OAuth Authorization Code on the server with offline access when background refresh is needed.
- Store refresh credentials encrypted server-side; never localStorage.
- Calendar account may differ from Supabase login account.
- Store selected calendar_id per organization/integration.
- External Google events are read-only by default.
- SerenaPsi-managed events are auditable/idempotent.
- Create Meet only using Calendar API `conferenceData.createRequest` with `conferenceSolutionKey.type="hangoutsMeet"`, request parameter `conferenceDataVersion=1`, and a new unique requestId for every new create attempt.
- Treat Meet creation as asynchronous: handle `pending`, `success`, and `failure`; re-fetch with bounded backoff and persist the URL only from a successful API response.
- Never fabricate a meet.google.com URL.
- Handle revoked refresh tokens and reconnect UX.
